  "notes": "Children start school at 4 in FS2 (Reception, left out as for England) and finish at 16 after GCSEs. The Infant and Junior School in Stanley and Camp Education teach FS1–Year 6; the Community School teaches Years 7–11, KS3 then GCSE courses in Years 10–11. There is no sixth form in the islands: the government funds two-year post-GCSE courses (A levels and other Level 3) in the UK, with funding capped at Peter Symonds College boarding costs, so Years 12–13 are listed as that route. The school year runs from September to early August."
